WEBVTT

00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:10.280
This is great!

00:00:12.430 --> 00:00:14.220
You can't swim there!

00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:15.720
Get back here!

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:21.010
A student council president doesn't even get to relax on a school trip.

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:29.830
This really is great!

00:00:37.190 --> 00:00:39.750
Nia, why don't you give up already?

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:41.170
Why don't you, Tomoharu?

00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:44.710
They're the same.

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:47.630
I can't lose to a little girl.

00:00:58.570 --> 00:00:59.500
It broke!

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:02.550
Is that the prize we won the other day?

00:01:02.830 --> 00:01:03.970
What's that doing here?

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:07.590
I didn't really want it around the house.

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:09.990
Wait a minute, Tomoharu!

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:12.550
Isn't that an Asura Machina plug-in?

00:01:12.870 --> 00:01:13.440
Huh?

00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:19.300
What are you doing, Tomo?

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:22.100
I didn't do anything!

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:23.480
Who are you kidding?

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:25.720
Why would I do something like that?

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:47.460
<i>Asura Cryin'</i>

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:04.650
"Until the End of the World"

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:08.740
Who's taking responsibility for this one?

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:12.730
Well, isn't the club president usually the one responsible...

00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:14.500
...for things that happen to the club room?

00:03:14.740 --> 00:03:15.660
The president?

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:17.000
Who is that, anyway?

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:18.640
Oh, yeah.

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:21.620
Shuri is only the acting president.

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:24.840
What is this plug-in?

00:03:28.010 --> 00:03:29.930
Class 1-7, Tomoharu Natsume.

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:32.340
Please come to the Third Student Council office immediately.

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:34.020
What? Me?

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:36.020
"Third Student Council"

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:39.880
I guess this is our first meeting face-to-face, Tomoharu Natsume.

00:03:40.310 --> 00:03:42.480
I've heard a lot about you.

00:03:43.730 --> 00:03:45.840
She can't have heard anything good.

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:48.720
I am Toru Kitsutaka...

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:51.270
...president of Rakurowa High School's Third Student Council.

00:03:51.510 --> 00:03:53.000
I see.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:56.130
I'm sure you know why you're here.

00:03:56.270 --> 00:03:58.340
Oh, um...

00:03:58.910 --> 00:04:01.890
You're the one that started that ruckus in the Science Club, aren't you?

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:03.910
Oh!

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:07.180
The students are slacking off...

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:09.250
...with the sophomores gone on their trip.

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:11.250
On top of that, summer vacation is coming up.

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:13.910
Little incidents occur every year.

00:04:14.150 --> 00:04:14.870
I see.

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:16.870
The Science Club is involved in something...

00:04:17.080 --> 00:04:18.520
...every year.

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:21.070
Watch yourself.

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:23.380
Yes. I'm sorry.

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:25.060
Good answer.

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:29.100
Tomo has nothing to with the Science Club's past.

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:29.870
Misao!

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:32.750
That's all, Tomoharu Natsume.

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:33.950
You can go.

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:35.440
Okay.

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:39.090
Misao!

00:04:39.530 --> 00:04:40.680
Fine, fine.

00:04:40.970 --> 00:04:44.810
So your projection body is called Misao.

00:04:45.290 --> 00:04:45.870
Huh?

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:47.070
Is she with you?

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:50.150
President Toru, are you...?

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:52.740
Go, Tomoharu Natsume.

00:05:04.420 --> 00:05:05.910
Have some tea.

00:05:06.630 --> 00:05:07.550
You shouldn't have.

00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:10.620
Sorry for dropping in on you on such short notice.

00:05:10.770 --> 00:05:11.730
It's fine.

00:05:12.110 --> 00:05:14.800
You're one of his friends, uh...

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:15.960
Kagakagari.

00:05:16.340 --> 00:05:17.400
Mr. Kagakagari.

00:05:18.070 --> 00:05:19.850
Oh, what beautiful roses!

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:21.390
Thank you.

00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:23.840
I should put them in some water.

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:27.930
There's no reason to keep them longer than you need to.

00:05:29.370 --> 00:05:30.620
This looks like fun.

00:05:31.960 --> 00:05:34.460
It was a fantastic party.

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:38.690
You should come next year if you can make it.

00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:41.000
It would be my pleasure.

00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:45.850
But you may not be able to host your party next year.

00:05:45.850 --> 00:05:46.430
What?

00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:47.780
Mrs. Kirie...

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:50.950
What would you do...

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:53.540
...if you got to see your daughter again?

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:56.380
What are we doing?

00:05:56.380 --> 00:05:59.360
Come on, hurry up.

00:05:59.550 --> 00:06:00.900
Good! Stay right there.

00:06:01.230 --> 00:06:03.300
Just stay there, Reishiro.

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:06.660
What are you planning, Shuri Kurosaki.

00:06:06.950 --> 00:06:08.660
Tomoharu asked me to do this.

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:09.880
Tomoharu Natsume?

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:15.170
Yes. He said this Polaroid camera is good for taking ghost pictures...

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:18.050
...so it might be able to take pictures of projection bodies.

00:06:18.580 --> 00:06:20.790
Reishiro, take one step to your right.

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:23.200
Projection bodies?

00:06:23.390 --> 00:06:25.550
We might get a picture of Aine.

00:06:26.030 --> 00:06:27.190
A picture of Aine?

00:06:27.430 --> 00:06:28.390
For what?

00:06:28.630 --> 00:06:32.670
You don't need a reason to take pictures.

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:33.770
Aine!

00:06:35.980 --> 00:06:38.910
Come on, smile!

00:06:40.020 --> 00:06:42.130
Hurry up and smile.

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:44.830
Don't make that sullen face, Aine.

00:06:44.830 --> 00:06:46.120
You've got to smile.

00:07:03.910 --> 00:07:05.540
What an awkward smile.

00:07:06.120 --> 00:07:07.370
Look who's talking.

00:07:14.430 --> 00:07:16.210
It'll be time for dinner soon.

00:07:16.550 --> 00:07:17.270
Let's go.

00:07:19.670 --> 00:07:20.250
Aine?

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:23.040
Just a little longer...

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:29.910
Okay.

00:07:33.130 --> 00:07:35.630
Do you think my mother would be happy...

00:07:35.820 --> 00:07:37.360
...to see this photo?

00:07:37.650 --> 00:07:41.110
I'm sure Kirie and Reiko would be very happy to see it.

00:07:41.490 --> 00:07:43.750
Kirie would turn it into a poster...

00:07:43.750 --> 00:07:45.380
...and put it up all over the neighborhood.

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:50.330
Let's show her when we get home.

00:07:52.690 --> 00:07:54.470
Yes, when we're home.

00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:06.390
Very well.

00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:09.130
I will begin my examination of this plug-in.

00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:10.670
Sure.

00:08:10.910 --> 00:08:14.410
Kanade, bring me hot milk in an hour.

00:08:15.900 --> 00:08:18.600
Do we really need to make Takatsuki stay here?

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:20.520
I can take care of the hot milk.

00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:24.070
Kanade makes the best hot milk.

00:08:26.960 --> 00:08:29.600
Yeah, the Splitter failed...

00:08:30.420 --> 00:08:32.730
...but I found an igniter.

00:08:33.110 --> 00:08:35.230
Your brother had it.

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:37.230
I guess I'm just lucky...

00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:39.690
...Naotaka Natsume.

00:08:44.260 --> 00:08:45.030
Kotori...

00:08:45.410 --> 00:08:46.950
...you were the one that showed me...

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:50.460
...in order to grow bigger, more beautiful flowers...

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:52.380
...they must be pruned.

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:55.270
I'll lose everything if I hesitate.

00:08:56.560 --> 00:08:59.020
It won't be long until the world ends...

00:08:59.980 --> 00:09:02.960
...so I'll pick them now.

00:09:08.870 --> 00:09:10.070
This time...

00:09:21.890 --> 00:09:22.810
Guess who.

00:09:23.430 --> 00:09:24.440
Shuri.

00:09:24.440 --> 00:09:25.980
Ding ding ding!

00:09:26.990 --> 00:09:28.620
Why are you calling me so early?

00:09:29.060 --> 00:09:30.450
How are things over there?

00:09:30.790 --> 00:09:31.840
Has anything happened?

00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:33.960
Changed? Oh!

00:09:34.390 --> 00:09:38.670
We found something that looks like an Asura Machina plug-in.

00:09:39.050 --> 00:09:45.350
Oh, my. I guess you'll have the Asura Cryin' after you again.

00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:46.170
What?

00:09:46.310 --> 00:09:50.590
Why don't you hand it over to President Toru?

00:09:50.680 --> 00:09:53.230
Huh? To her?

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:57.410
Yeah, she's got her act together, so I'm sure she can help you.

00:09:58.760 --> 00:10:03.560
I'll be coming back on tomorrow's Northeast flight 993...

00:10:03.560 --> 00:10:06.880
...so try to take care of everything before I'm back.

00:10:13.850 --> 00:10:14.710
Tomoharu.

00:10:16.010 --> 00:10:16.880
Takatsuki.

00:10:17.930 --> 00:10:19.090
What are you doing?

00:10:19.520 --> 00:10:21.490
Shuri woke me with a phone call.

00:10:22.930 --> 00:10:23.700
What about you?

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:25.770
I came to get some water.

00:10:26.110 --> 00:10:26.780
I see.

00:10:31.580 --> 00:10:32.830
The Asura Cryin'...

00:10:33.800 --> 00:10:34.830
Kagakagari...

00:10:35.330 --> 00:10:38.120
...might come after the plug-in.

00:10:38.650 --> 00:10:39.510
What?

00:10:45.140 --> 00:10:47.300
Promise me.

00:10:47.590 --> 00:10:48.450
Promise?

00:10:48.980 --> 00:10:50.520
That you won't fight again.

00:10:51.390 --> 00:10:53.890
That you won't use the Asura Machina.

00:10:55.900 --> 00:10:57.300
Please promise me.

00:11:03.980 --> 00:11:07.100
Are you really giving that to President Toru?

00:11:07.580 --> 00:11:09.510
I'm not done with my examination.

00:11:09.990 --> 00:11:10.800
It's better this way.

00:11:11.190 --> 00:11:13.400
Holding on to this mysterious plug-in...

00:11:13.780 --> 00:11:15.850
...will only get me in trouble.

00:11:15.850 --> 00:11:16.330
Tomo!

00:11:20.940 --> 00:11:22.480
Hey, boy.

00:11:22.770 --> 00:11:23.780
Kagakagari!

00:11:36.180 --> 00:11:37.380
We meet again.

00:11:38.050 --> 00:11:40.030
Give me the igniter.

00:11:40.550 --> 00:11:41.560
Igniter?

00:11:41.710 --> 00:11:43.390
It's that thing you're holding.

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:45.120
Give it to me.

00:11:45.460 --> 00:11:48.390
There's no point in you holding on to it.

00:11:48.820 --> 00:11:50.550
Are you up to something again?

00:11:50.740 --> 00:11:51.370
Yes.

00:11:51.850 --> 00:11:53.390
Something like demon hunting?

00:11:53.720 --> 00:11:54.880
Could be.

00:11:56.560 --> 00:11:57.330
I can't give this to you.

00:11:58.340 --> 00:11:59.330
So that's how it'll be.

00:11:59.780 --> 00:12:00.550
Ingrid.

00:12:03.620 --> 00:12:04.390
Run!

00:12:06.700 --> 00:12:07.760
I won't let you.

00:12:11.070 --> 00:12:11.990
President Rikka!

00:12:13.140 --> 00:12:14.530
W-wait, what?

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:20.250
Suisho, showdown!

00:12:28.860 --> 00:12:30.110
What's going on?

00:12:30.250 --> 00:12:31.500
I'll explain later!

00:12:42.790 --> 00:12:45.490
This isn't going to be cheap, Tomoharu Natsume.

00:12:46.400 --> 00:12:47.940
I don't know who you are...

00:12:48.230 --> 00:12:50.480
...but don't you think you're being rude?

00:12:50.920 --> 00:12:53.030
Then in lieu of introductions...

00:13:03.130 --> 00:13:04.570
Circulation of magic?

00:13:04.810 --> 00:13:07.070
You're an Asura Cryin'?

00:13:13.840 --> 00:13:14.760
President Rikka!

00:13:17.780 --> 00:13:18.550
Engetsu!

00:13:24.130 --> 00:13:25.380
That won't work, Kanade!

00:13:25.620 --> 00:13:28.070
A slime will regenerate immediately if it's cut!

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:29.370
In that case...

00:13:30.040 --> 00:13:31.100
Wait, Takatsuki!

00:13:32.440 --> 00:13:33.740
Kurogane and I will do it!

00:13:34.510 --> 00:13:35.090
No!

00:13:35.950 --> 00:13:37.300
You must not fight!

00:13:37.540 --> 00:13:38.690
But...

00:13:47.490 --> 00:13:48.210
Takatsuki!

00:13:53.400 --> 00:13:54.890
Come, Kurogane!

00:13:55.660 --> 00:13:58.350
From the abyss deeper than darkness.

00:13:58.730 --> 00:14:01.860
The shadow cast by the light of science.

00:14:10.890 --> 00:14:12.430
No!

00:14:15.410 --> 00:14:17.000
No!

00:14:30.360 --> 00:14:31.990
Touo, draw.

00:14:32.760 --> 00:14:33.530
You!

00:14:38.340 --> 00:14:39.150
Well.

00:14:40.740 --> 00:14:41.850
I see.

00:14:44.390 --> 00:14:45.980
It seems I'm at a disadvantage.

00:14:48.910 --> 00:14:49.630
President Toru!

00:15:00.210 --> 00:15:03.430
Wow! What is she?

00:15:06.890 --> 00:15:08.760
Takatsuki, what's wrong?

00:15:10.390 --> 00:15:12.610
You promised.

00:15:12.940 --> 00:15:13.470
Huh?

00:15:13.950 --> 00:15:17.220
You promised you wouldn't fight.

00:15:17.410 --> 00:15:18.330
Oh!

00:15:19.140 --> 00:15:22.120
You promised you wouldn't fight!

00:15:31.730 --> 00:15:33.750
You made her cry.

00:15:39.470 --> 00:15:43.510
Why don't you explain what's going on, Tomoharu Natsume.

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:45.510
Oh, uh...

00:15:45.770 --> 00:15:46.920
This is the reason behind this.

00:15:47.500 --> 00:15:48.170
What is it?

00:15:48.460 --> 00:15:50.290
An Asura Machina plug-in.

00:15:50.430 --> 00:15:52.980
Kagakagari called it an igniter.

00:15:53.170 --> 00:15:54.180
Igniter?

00:15:54.950 --> 00:15:56.920
So that's what he's after?

00:15:57.300 --> 00:15:57.980
Yes.

00:15:57.980 --> 00:16:00.570
So it's something amazing?

00:16:00.570 --> 00:16:02.780
Do you think it would sell for a lot?

00:16:03.460 --> 00:16:04.270
I don't know.

00:16:04.270 --> 00:16:04.850
What?

00:16:05.430 --> 00:16:08.890
The igniter doesn't fit with any existing Asura Machina.

00:16:09.510 --> 00:16:10.890
Its build is different.

00:16:11.340 --> 00:16:13.550
Even if you use it with an existing machine...

00:16:14.080 --> 00:16:16.050
...it won't function.

00:16:18.260 --> 00:16:19.220
That's odd.

00:16:19.650 --> 00:16:22.730
Why would Kagakagari be after something like that?

00:16:22.970 --> 00:16:25.040
I bet it's one of those.

00:16:25.230 --> 00:16:27.730
It must be extremely valuable.

00:16:27.730 --> 00:16:30.710
A collector's item.

00:16:30.950 --> 00:16:34.460
President Rikka, is all you can think about selling it?

00:16:34.650 --> 00:16:36.280
Of course.

00:16:36.430 --> 00:16:38.640
It's my fee for rescuing you just now.

00:16:38.880 --> 00:16:40.850
I told you it wouldn't be cheap.

00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:42.870
You did say something like that.

00:16:43.060 --> 00:16:46.760
So the Second Student Council will be taking this.

00:16:47.240 --> 00:16:47.910
No.

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:53.970
If you do that, the igniter could end up with Kagakagari at any time.

00:16:56.320 --> 00:16:58.920
Then why don't you hold on to it, President Toru?

00:17:00.170 --> 00:17:03.340
You're right. I'll keep this.

00:17:25.210 --> 00:17:27.810
Kanade, I'll leave a towel for you here.

00:17:28.090 --> 00:17:29.390
Thank you.

00:17:34.680 --> 00:17:37.230
Kanade, I'm sure you know.

00:17:38.040 --> 00:17:41.650
If you keep using your power without a contractor...

00:17:43.470 --> 00:17:44.340
Kanade!

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:47.370
Yes, I know.

00:17:58.610 --> 00:18:00.920
What are you moping about?

00:18:01.160 --> 00:18:02.360
What do you mean?

00:18:02.650 --> 00:18:04.720
It's because you made Kanade cry, right?

00:18:09.140 --> 00:18:12.120
Why do you think she cried, Tomoharu?

00:18:12.410 --> 00:18:13.030
Huh?

00:18:13.370 --> 00:18:16.490
Because I ignored her...

00:18:16.780 --> 00:18:20.430
...and tried to fight Kagakagari?

00:18:20.670 --> 00:18:21.350
Probably.

00:18:21.680 --> 00:18:23.940
Demons don't cry easily.

00:18:24.130 --> 00:18:26.150
Huh? Why, then?

00:18:26.830 --> 00:18:30.190
She couldn't explain even if she wanted to.

00:18:30.620 --> 00:18:32.640
If she told you...

00:18:32.980 --> 00:18:36.290
...you wouldn't be able to protect yourself any more.

00:18:38.360 --> 00:18:41.290
Nia, I don't get what you're trying to say.

00:18:41.580 --> 00:18:42.640
I thought so.

00:18:42.980 --> 00:18:46.440
That's why the hot milk you make is too sweet.

00:18:46.630 --> 00:18:47.400
What?

00:18:47.590 --> 00:18:48.310
What are you talking about?

00:18:48.740 --> 00:18:51.960
Just give her some space.

00:18:52.160 --> 00:18:55.280
I don't think Kanade wants to see you right now.

00:18:55.380 --> 00:18:56.820
Huh? Why not?

00:18:57.110 --> 00:18:58.500
Isn't it obvious?

00:18:58.790 --> 00:19:04.360
I don't think she'd want to be asked about why she cried.

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:05.320
Huh?

00:19:06.000 --> 00:19:09.310
I guess so.

00:19:09.840 --> 00:19:13.010
There's no point in worrying about it.

00:19:13.500 --> 00:19:16.570
When Kanade calms down, you can go talk to her...

00:19:16.570 --> 00:19:18.730
...and sort this all out!

00:19:19.120 --> 00:19:19.840
Right?

00:19:20.270 --> 00:19:22.920
Why do you always have so much energy?

00:19:23.350 --> 00:19:26.470
If I have energy, then you'll have energy, too!

00:19:32.580 --> 00:19:33.390
I guess so.

00:19:40.550 --> 00:19:42.240
Please...

00:19:42.720 --> 00:19:46.660
Please save us...

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:49.450
Aine?

00:19:50.210 --> 00:19:53.960
What was Reishiro Saeki's projection body doing here?

00:19:55.120 --> 00:19:58.190
We interrupt this program for this emergency news report.

00:19:59.050 --> 00:20:08.470
"Northeast flight from Honolulu disappears"

00:19:59.540 --> 00:20:04.100
This evening, Northeast Airlines flight 933 departing from Honolulu...

00:20:04.100 --> 00:20:08.430
...for Kanto International airport has ceased communications.

00:20:08.720 --> 00:20:09.300
Huh?

00:20:10.500 --> 00:20:13.480
Isn't this Shuri's flight?

00:20:14.100 --> 00:20:14.970
It is.

00:20:17.560 --> 00:20:18.280
What is this?

00:20:18.760 --> 00:20:20.450
What's going on?

00:20:24.000 --> 00:20:26.120
No... Reishiro.

00:20:34.380 --> 00:20:37.890
So people are doomed to repeat their actions.

00:20:38.610 --> 00:20:41.020
What will you do...

00:20:41.310 --> 00:20:44.000
...when you discover the truth of this world?

00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:50.870
Good evening!

00:20:51.640 --> 00:20:56.540
I'm here to collect President Rikka's rescue fee.

00:20:57.020 --> 00:20:58.180
What's going on?

00:21:04.180 --> 00:21:06.060
Let's make a deal, boy.

00:21:06.390 --> 00:21:07.210
Kagakagari!

00:21:07.500 --> 00:21:09.090
W-what?

00:21:09.810 --> 00:21:12.260
I have your sophomores.

00:21:13.170 --> 00:21:15.430
Do you mean you're behind this?

00:21:15.770 --> 00:21:16.730
Don't worry.

00:21:17.210 --> 00:21:18.840
If you give me the igniter...

00:21:18.840 --> 00:21:21.150
...I'll release all the hostages.

00:21:21.440 --> 00:21:22.880
W-wait a minute!

00:21:22.880 --> 00:21:24.270
I'll call you again.

00:21:24.370 --> 00:21:26.000
I don't have it any more!

00:21:26.200 --> 00:21:27.590
Then get it.

00:23:19.910 --> 00:23:24.860
"Preview"

00:23:21.160 --> 00:23:21.880
Good bye.

00:23:22.270 --> 00:23:22.800
No.

00:23:23.130 --> 00:23:24.000
I have to do it.

00:23:24.380 --> 00:23:25.010
Why?

00:23:25.440 --> 00:23:26.400
Don't cry.

00:23:26.500 --> 00:23:28.130
Always and forever.

00:23:28.560 --> 00:23:29.190
I'm sorry.

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:30.300
Thank you.

00:23:31.510 --> 00:23:34.960
"Mark of the Cursed Criminal"
